accordin Pakistan has sentenced a  university lecturer to death for  blasphemy  Junaid Hafiz was arrested in 2013  accused of insulting the Prophet  Mohammed on Facebook he spent nearly six  years in solitary confinement waiting  for his trial on Pakistan's  controversial blasphemy law carries an  automatic death penalty it's yet to be  actually be carried out but the law has  drawn widespread condemnation from  rights groups as , Haider explains from  Islamabad Junaid Hafiz came to Pakistan  from the US and was hired as an English  literature professor he's a Fulbright  Scholar and of course has also earned  praise for his academic work however a  group of students then objected to his  Facebook page accused him of blasphemy  in 2013 he was arrested and charged with  blasphemy under Pakistan's law 295 C of  the Penal Code that is the Pakistan  Penal Code anyone who defies the name of  the Prophet as it provides for a  sentence of death in this particular  case Hafeez had been in jail since 2013  it's been six long years a number of the  judges have already been changed and  today the verdict was read out on the  maximum security inside the prison  because back in 2014 his lawyer was  gunned down and so he of course  according to reports was kept in  solitary confinement because of fear for  his life but that particular judgment  coming out inside the jail in Multan
 

